'' A MODULE THAT EXPANDS __TIME__ IS NEVER STORED (tiko-build B0, 2026-10-11). It was: the
'' second build hit, linked the first build's object, and printed the first build's time
'' beside the root's current one. Both builds must miss, and neither may store; the module
'' with no clock beside it still stores and hits, so the cache itself is on.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.mct-clock/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' CLEAN: build/.mct-clock
'' COPY: tests/modules/src/clock => build/.mct-clock
'' STEP: -v -target win64-msvc -i build/.mct-clock/libs build/.mct-clock/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-clock/app.exe
'' STEP-OUT: module acme.stamp: not stored
'' ARGS: -v -target win64-msvc -i build/.mct-clock/libs build/.mct-clock/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-clock/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.plain: hit
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.stamp: miss (new)
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.stamp: not stored
'' EXPECT-NOT: module acme.stamp: hit
'' RUN: build/.mct-clock/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  8 2
